Person Responsible: Annette Carper, Executive Director

2023-027: Wyoming Office of State Lands and Investments (OSLI) - Activities Allowed or Unallowed and Cash Management (Material Weakness; Noncompliance)

Corrective actions: The Disbursement Specialist reviews the Loan Draft Requests (LDR) and verifies the expenditures to supporting documentation submitted with the requests for accuracy and allowable costs. If satisfied, the Disbursement Specialist signs and dates the LDRs indicating financial approval for payment. The DEQ Senior Engineer or DEQ Principal Engineer performs technical reviews of the draft requests for eligibility of all costs. The technical reviewer signs and returns the LDR to OSLI. Upon receipt by OSLI, the Disbursement Specialist then enters the transaction into EnABLE and the WOLFS accounting system for payment. EnABLE and WOLFS are not integrated.

Following the established review process of the LDRs, the Disbursement Specialist updates, prepares, and provides the following items when disbursements for first-round funds are being reviewed and approved in EnABLE and WOLFS. This is to ensure the funds are being drawn from the correct grant and program. All payment entries in EnABLE are approved by the Grants & Loans Manager, Assistant Director, or Financial Reporting Manager (agency).

•	Reviewed/signed LDR;
•	Loan LOC (each loan has its own spreadsheet detailing from which source the loan is funded);
•	Updated Sum Sheet (which is compared to the loan LOC to ensure the correct funding source); 
•	Updated Cash Draw and CD Sheets recording from which grant the funds were drawn (utilizing the FIFO method);
•	GAX printout from WOLFS to verify the budget coding in WOLFS is correct (to be signed and dated by the approver);
•	EnABLE printout of pending transaction to be approved (to be signed by the approver); and
•	A draft CR printed from WOLFS verifying the budget coding for when the funds are deposited from ASAP. 

For LDRs funded from second-round funds, the process is the same, except that the items provided to the approver are limited to:

•	Reviewed/signed LDR;
•	Loan LOC (each loan has its own spreadsheet detailing from which source the loan is funded);
•	GAX printout from WOLFS to verify the budget coding in WOLFS is correct (to be signed and dated by the approver); and
•	EnABLE printout of pending transaction to be approved (to be signed by the approver).

Anticipated completion date: December 31, 2023

Contact person: Beth Blackwell, Grants and Loans Manager

